  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Marathon Petroleum obligated $503M in FY2026 to date in federal contract obligations. Marathon Petroleum received 140 awards so far in the fiscal year, with an average award size of $3.6M. Obligations fell 7.2% year over year. Marathon Petroleum’s federal obligations have trended up and down over the past six fiscal years: FY21 obligations were $11.9M, FY22 obligations were $93.1M, FY23 obligations were $359M, FY24 obligations were $288M, FY25 obligations were $542M, and FY26 obligations are $503M to date. The current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date figures rather than full-year totals. The note clarifies that all figures are contract obligations except award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables, which are total contract values. The count of 140 awards and the average award size of $3.6M provide a sense of deal scale for the current fiscal year. Use the fiscal-year series to see how procurement volume has shifted across FY21 through FY26 to date.",
